Products.DisableXMLRPC
=====================

Disable Zope's built-in XML-RPC support on older Zope versions.

Zope 5.13 introduced the ``enable-xmlrpc`` directive in ``zope.conf``:
when set to ``off``, every ``POST`` request with ``Content-Type: text/xml``
(i.e. an XML-RPC call) is rejected with ``400 Bad Request: Unsupported
request type``. XML-RPC is rarely used nowadays and is a common target
for abuse (brute force, amplification, ...).

This product backports the same behaviour to:

* Zope2 2.13 (Plone 4.x, Python 2.7)
* Zope 4.x (Plone 5.2, Python 2.7 and 3)
* Zope 5.x < 5.13 (Plone 6.0 / 6.1, Python 3)

On Zope >= 5.13 the product does nothing (it only logs a message): use the
native directive instead::

    enable-xmlrpc off


How it works
------------

In all these versions ``HTTPRequest.processInputs`` uses the module global
``ZPublisher.HTTPRequest.xmlrpc`` to parse XML-RPC calls. The product
replaces it with a small proxy that raises ``zExceptions.BadRequest('Unsupported
request type')`` when XML-RPC is disabled, and delegates to the original
``ZPublisher.xmlrpc`` module otherwise. ``processInputs`` itself is not
patched.

The patch is applied when the product is imported, which Zope does at
startup for every package in the ``Products`` namespace: no ZCML and no
add-on activation are needed.


Installation
------------

**XML-RPC is disabled as soon as the product is installed.**

Buildout (Plone 4.x / 5.x)::

    [instance]
    eggs =
        ...
        Products.DisableXMLRPC

pip::

    pip install Products.DisableXMLRPC

On Zope2 2.13 you can also simply copy the ``src/Products/DisableXMLRPC``
folder into the instance ``products`` directory. This does not work on
Zope 4/5 under WSGI, where the ``products`` directive no longer exists.

At startup you should see in the log::

    INFO Products.DisableXMLRPC XML-RPC support patched (currently disabled). ...


Configuration
-------------

XML-RPC can be re-enabled, in order of precedence:

1. with the ``ZOPE_ENABLE_XMLRPC`` environment variable
   (``on``/``off``, ``true``/``false``, ``yes``/``no``, ``1``/``0``);

2. with a ``product-config`` section in ``zope.conf``::

       <product-config disable-xmlrpc>
           enable-xmlrpc on
       </product-config>

   With ``plone.recipe.zope2instance``::

       [instance]
       zope-conf-additional =
           <product-config disable-xmlrpc>
               enable-xmlrpc on
           </product-config>

3. otherwise XML-RPC is **disabled**.


Testing it
----------

::

    curl -i -X POST -H 'Content-Type: text/xml' \
        --data '<?xml version="1.0"?><methodCall><methodName>getId</methodName></methodCall>' \
        http://localhost:8080/Plone

returns ``400 Bad Request`` while XML-RPC is disabled.


Running the tests
-----------------

::

    tox

Environments: ``py27-zope213`` (Zope2 2.13), ``py27-zope4``,
``py38-zope4``, ``py311-zope512`` and ``py311-zope513`` (native support,
the patch must not be applied).


